.TH HALCYON-CTL 1 "2026-11-11" "Halcyon 0.6.5" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
halcyon-ctl \- control Halcyon desktop widgets
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B halcyon-ctl
.RI [ command ]
.RI [ arguments ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Control Halcyon from the terminal or a desktop shortcut.
Run with no command to open Settings.
.B halcyon-ctl
.I command
.B --help
describes one command.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B start
Show the widgets now and at every sign-in.
.TP
.B stop
Hide the widgets and stop starting them at sign-in.
.TP
.B restart
Restart the widgets, for example after an update.
.TP
.B status
Show whether the widgets are running.
.TP
.BI "settings \fR[\fB--page " page\fR]
Open Settings, on
.I page
if given (for example
.BR clock ).
.TP
.B drawer
Open or close the edge menu, the same as
.BR "halcyon --toggle drawer" .
.TP
.BI "panel \fR[\fIwidget\fR|\fBopen\fR|\fBclose\fR|\fBrail\fR]"
Open the edge menu, or open it on one widget.
.TP
.BI toggle " widget"
Show or hide one widget.
.TP
.BI focus " action"
Control the Focus timer, for example from a keyboard shortcut.
.TP
.BI theme " name"
Apply a Halcyon theme.
.TP
.BR cosmic-colors " on|off"
Turn matching the COSMIC accent color on or off.
.TP
.BI weather " city"
Set the weather city by name.
.TP
.B weather-picker
Choose the weather city in Settings.
.TP
.B restore
Put back your wallpaper from before Halcyon and stop the widgets.
This also stops them starting at sign-in; run
.B halcyon-ctl start
to turn them back on.
.TP
.B restore-wallpaper
Put back only your wallpaper from before Halcyon.
.TP
.B wallpapers-install
Check that Halcyon's built-in wallpapers are installed.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR halcyon (1)
.br
https://github.com/profilaz3/halcyon
